# Preferences

How you want to be worked with. Claude reads this at the start of any session that writes code.
Delete what does not apply and add what does.

## Communication

- Plain words. Explain a diagram rather than writing three paragraphs.
- Say what changed and what is still broken. Do not hedge finished work.

## Before acting

- Discuss anything with judgement in it: a new lane's name, scope, or approach.
- Run read-only things freely.

## Commits and branches

- Ask before committing.
- Commits are coherent units, not one per edit and not one giant one.
- Never push to a default branch without being told.

## Code

- Match the surrounding style rather than importing your own.
- Say when a change needs a test, and write it.
